(314480, 23370, 7504, '<td valign="top">I think this would say "sound" to me more, if someone was actually playing the trumpet.  : )  Cool effect though, I like it!</td>', 'I think this would say "sound" to me more, if someone was actually playing the trumpet.  : )  Cool effect though, I like it!', '2003-06-04 00:25:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(314483, 23516, 7504, '<td valign="top">Yeah, I can hear that sizzling, and smell it too, mmm.  Nice idea!</td>', 'Yeah, I can hear that sizzling, and smell it too, mmm.  Nice idea!', '2003-06-04 00:27:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(314486, 23472, 7504, '<td valign="top">Hmm, I guess I don''t understand this one for "sound", but I like the digtal effects and the artistic composition.   Sorry, to be dense, but I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt and figure it''s about sound. : )</td>', 'Hmm, I guess I don''t understand this one for "sound", but I like the digtal effects and the artistic composition.   Sorry, to be dense, but I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt and figure it''s about sound. : )', '2003-06-04 00:30:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(314661, 23185, 8530, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid I''m not totally clear on what that is, even if the earmuffs do suggest it''s some sort of machinery, so I can''t tell how well this really meets the challenge. The tone on the photo is a nice touch but I wish I had a better clue what was going on here.</td>', 'I''m afraid I''m not totally clear on what that is, even if the earmuffs do suggest it''s some sort of machinery, so I can''t tell how well this really meets the challenge. The tone on the photo is a nice touch but I wish I had a better clue what was going on here.', '2003-06-04 02:42:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(314662, 23127, 8530, '<td valign="top">I think I would have preferred this without the reflective surface. The rest is fine -- the folds maybe show a little too much in your backdrop but the contrast between it and the pins helps alleviate that... it does meet the topic.</td>', 'I think I would have preferred this without the reflective surface. The rest is fine -- the folds maybe show a little too much in your backdrop but the contrast between it and the pins helps alleviate that... it does meet the topic.', '2003-06-04 02:43:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(314665, 23466, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hmm, curious how you set this up. It works with the topic. That glare in the center is unfortunately high, very disruptive in a photo otherwise fairly dark.</td>', 'Hmm, curious how you set this up. It works with the topic. That glare in the center is unfortunately high, very disruptive in a photo otherwise fairly dark.', '2003-06-04 02:45:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(314666, 23503, 8530, '<td valign="top">Without the title I would just say ''too blurry'' and move on. With the title, I''m wondering if you were trying for the motion of the speaker. It works for the topic, although it''s not something that terribly grabs my interest. The contrast is a little on the harsh side, and the lighting reflection just makes things look more blurry.</td>', 'Without the title I would just say ''too blurry'' and move on. With the title, I''m wondering if you were trying for the motion of the speaker. It works for the topic, although it''s not something that terribly grabs my interest. The contrast is a little on the harsh side, and the lighting reflection just makes things look more blurry.', '2003-06-04 02:46:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(314670, 22971, 8682, '<td valign="top">beatiful... and good details</td>', 'beatiful... and good details', '2003-06-04 02:48:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(314673, 22925, 8530, '<td valign="top">This does work in terms of topic but I think I would have preferred either a tighter focus on the moving car or a shot encompassing a larger portion of the roller coaster. There''s some graininess around the (electrical?) lines at the top and a little patchiness in the sky in general -- jpeg artifacts?</td>', 'This does work in terms of topic but I think I would have preferred either a tighter focus on the moving car or a shot encompassing a larger portion of the roller coaster. There''s some graininess around the (electrical?) lines at the top and a little patchiness in the sky in general -- jpeg artifacts?', '2003-06-04 02:49:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(314675, 23526, 8530, '<td valign="top">*rubs ear* Okay! It''s a good job when I really DO hear it in my mind!<br/> <br/>Nice motion capture. Why black and white, though? One of the things I like about cymbals is their visual tone is as bright as their aural one.</td>', '*rubs ear* Okay! It''s a good job when I really DO hear it in my mind! Nice motion capture. Why black and white, though? One of the things I like about cymbals is their visual tone is as bright as their aural one.', '2003-06-04 02:50:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(314676, 23547, 8530, '<td valign="top">HOME ALONE 37!<br/> <br/>*ahem* Pardon me. It does meet the topic, but it''s a little on the bland side -- white shirt and pale background and even the paleness of the skin on the left side. This may have been deliberate to emphasize the mouth but as the neutral space takes up so much of the photo it works against that in my view.</td>', 'HOME ALONE 37! *ahem* Pardon me. It does meet the topic, but it''s a little on the bland side -- white shirt and pale background and even the paleness of the skin on the left side. This may have been deliberate to emphasize the mouth but as the neutral space takes up so much of the photo it works against that in my view.', '2003-06-04 02:51:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(314677, 23513, 8530, '<td valign="top">Very, very, very, very, very distracting internal border.<br/> <br/>Highlights on the brass maybe a bit too bright. Focus is an interesting choice; you almost can''t tell if it''s currently being played or not, which is good as the static musical instrument shots didn''t grab me as well in terms of topic.</td>', 'Very, very, very, very, very distracting internal border. Highlights on the brass maybe a bit too bright. Focus is an interesting choice; you almost can''t tell if it''s currently being played or not, which is good as the static musical instrument shots didn''t grab me as well in terms of topic.', '2003-06-04 02:53:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(314679, 23308, 8530, '<td valign="top">I wish the focus were tighter on the vibration with less space to the left taken up by the rest of the fiddle. Works well with the topic.</td>', 'I wish the focus were tighter on the vibration with less space to the left taken up by the rest of the fiddle. Works well with the topic.', '2003-06-04 02:54:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(314680, 23384, 8530, '<td valign="top">All y''all with piano shots really are going to have to tell me what you''re playing. :)<br/> <br/>This is nice, particularly the lighting. It looks much like I''d expect in a concert hall setting, in fact, though I''m not sure why that is -- maybe it''s a soft-spot similarity.</td>', 'All y''all with piano shots really are going to have to tell me what you''re playing. :) This is nice, particularly the lighting. It looks much like I''d expect in a concert hall setting, in fact, though I''m not sure why that is -- maybe it''s a soft-spot similarity.', '2003-06-04 02:56:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(314681, 23527, 8530, '<td valign="top">Heh, I was wondering if I still had my old ankle bells but I couldn''t find them. Nice choice IMO therefore. A slightly different pose with the feet further apart might have given a bit more emphasis to the concept of motion and therefore ringing but it''s certainly not absent with the feet in the position they are, I''m just nitpicking.<br/> <br/>I''m a little uncertain why you chose B&amp;W for this as all the traditional dances I can think of involving bells are things that involve very colourful costumery; I don''t think it would have distracted but rather helped. However, that rug might be colourful enough to prove me wrong.</td>', 'Heh, I was wondering if I still had my old ankle bells but I couldn''t find them. Nice choice IMO therefore. A slightly different pose with the feet further apart might have given a bit more emphasis to the concept of motion and therefore ringing but it''s certainly not absent with the feet in the position they are, I''m just nitpicking. I''m a little uncertain why you chose B&W for this as all the traditional dances I can think of involving bells are things that involve very colourful costumery; I don''t think it would have distracted but rather helped. However, that rug might be colourful enough to prove me wrong.', '2003-06-04 02:58:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(314682, 23549, 8530, '<td valign="top">I know it''s hard to capture glass shots and not miss the glass, but that very bright background just makes it tougher to pick up; I would have liked more contrast.</td>', 'I know it''s hard to capture glass shots and not miss the glass, but that very bright background just makes it tougher to pick up; I would have liked more contrast.', '2003-06-04 02:59:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(314684, 23523, 8530, '<td valign="top">One whole balloon earlier, one already dead one now -- makes me REALLY want to see the stage in between in a motion capture. I like the shot anyhow; the falling motion is obvious as if the pop was recent, which helps with the challenge topic being met. Maybe too bright on the lighting on top -- it probably helped make a nice crisp shadow, so only ''maybe'', but it''s a little distracting.</td>', 'One whole balloon earlier, one already dead one now -- makes me REALLY want to see the stage in between in a motion capture. I like the shot anyhow; the falling motion is obvious as if the pop was recent, which helps with the challenge topic being met. Maybe too bright on the lighting on top -- it probably helped make a nice crisp shadow, so only ''maybe'', but it''s a little distracting.', '2003-06-04 03:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(314686, 22855, 8530, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure the arm:face ratio in this shot is the best choice, and I''m quite certain I would have preferred a darker background for more contrast between it and the skin. I see the relation to the topic but it wasn''t an instant impact of ''sound'', it took a moment to settle in.</td>', 'I''m not sure the arm:face ratio in this shot is the best choice, and I''m quite certain I would have preferred a darker background for more contrast between it and the skin. I see the relation to the topic but it wasn''t an instant impact of ''sound'', it took a moment to settle in.', '2003-06-04 03:04:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(314690, 23370, 8530, '<td valign="top">*tilts head* How did you do this? Well, hopefully it''ll be obvious post-challenge.<br/> <br/>The problem for me with the concept of this photo is that as the trumpet is not currently being played, the fingers-in-ears thing is less of a good match. The basic concept is sound, it''s the precise implementation that I''m not as keen on.</td>', '*tilts head* How did you do this? Well, hopefully it''ll be obvious post-challenge. The problem for me with the concept of this photo is that as the trumpet is not currently being played, the fingers-in-ears thing is less of a good match. The basic concept is sound, it''s the precise implementation that I''m not as keen on.', '2003-06-04 03:06:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(314694, 23511, 8530, '<td valign="top">Paper megaphone? Interesting choice. It connects to the topic after a moment''s thought. I like the tunnel-to-lips shot rather than some other depiction, much more interesting than a side shot or something similar would be.</td>', 'Paper megaphone? Interesting choice. It connects to the topic after a moment''s thought. I like the tunnel-to-lips shot rather than some other depiction, much more interesting than a side shot or something similar would be.', '2003-06-04 03:09:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(314699, 22840, 8530, '<td valign="top">I''d say "It''s Mardi Gras!" except, of course, it can''t be. However, I am curious what it is.<br/> <br/>"Loud colours" is right. This photo is very busy and seems somewhat out of focus. I see the double-display of the challenge topic but the composition is sufficiently distracting that it''s not a terribly attractive photo to me.</td>', 'I''d say "It''s Mardi Gras!" except, of course, it can''t be. However, I am curious what it is. "Loud colours" is right. This photo is very busy and seems somewhat out of focus. I see the double-display of the challenge topic but the composition is sufficiently distracting that it''s not a terribly attractive photo to me.', '2003-06-04 03:10:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(314701, 23533, 8530, '<td valign="top">I think it''s almost as surprising someone still owns a radio of that sort as the folks who have phonographs. It works for the topic, but I''m not sure how I feel about the motion in the shot; on the one hand, I can see someone carrying the radio and doing a little dancing along, but on the other a crisper shot might have been preferable.<br/> <br/>The contrast between everything but the radio parts is low, which along with the blur is somewhat distracting.</td>', 'I think it''s almost as surprising someone still owns a radio of that sort as the folks who have phonographs. It works for the topic, but I''m not sure how I feel about the motion in the shot; on the one hand, I can see someone carrying the radio and doing a little dancing along, but on the other a crisper shot might have been preferable. The contrast between everything but the radio parts is low, which along with the blur is somewhat distracting.', '2003-06-04 03:12:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(314704, 23536, 8530, '<td valign="top">I had to scroll my eyes over a great deal of bright and eye-catching colour before finding the bee, which doesn''t help with the feel of ''sound''. A tighter focus on the bee or a less bright set of flowers or even some less bright lighting might have helped with this. The border is very distracting as is; either a solid one or none at all would have been preferable.</td>', 'I had to scroll my eyes over a great deal of bright and eye-catching colour before finding the bee, which doesn''t help with the feel of ''sound''. A tighter focus on the bee or a less bright set of flowers or even some less bright lighting might have helped with this. The border is very distracting as is; either a solid one or none at all would have been preferable.', '2003-06-04 03:14:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(314706, 23520, 8530, '<td valign="top">Mmm... while I agree waves goes with the topic, the ones in this are a little on the wimpy side and the presence of the surfers ends up being distracting because of it. More background waves of a larger sort -- or even waves crashing over the boarding surfers'' heads -- would have helped this impression. Also the extreme brightness of the shot really washes out the majority of the waves.</td>', 'Mmm... while I agree waves goes with the topic, the ones in this are a little on the wimpy side and the presence of the surfers ends up being distracting because of it. More background waves of a larger sort -- or even waves crashing over the boarding surfers'' heads -- would have helped this impression. Also the extreme brightness of the shot really washes out the majority of the waves.', '2003-06-04 03:16:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(314709, 23509, 8530, '<td valign="top">Static whistle not as sound-conveying as active one. It meets the challenge but not intently. Picture itself is okay, good use of contrasting background, but not terribly interesting to me.</td>', 'Static whistle not as sound-conveying as active one. It meets the challenge but not intently. Picture itself is okay, good use of contrasting background, but not terribly interesting to me.', '2003-06-04 03:18:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(314721, 23538, 8530, '<td valign="top">I do not care for the overall orangey tone of the shot, though I don''t know how avoidable that might have been depending on lighting. The actual concept is good one... hey, wait. Is that a Hot Wheels?</td>', 'I do not care for the overall orangey tone of the shot, though I don''t know how avoidable that might have been depending on lighting. The actual concept is good one... hey, wait. Is that a Hot Wheels?', '2003-06-04 03:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(314730, 23463, 8530, '<td valign="top">I will not argue about whether or not this is a ''sound''. Look, I''m shutting up about it right now.<br/> <br/>It''s a very pretty photograph. I like the line of powerline poles and the dip and swap that follows the mountain for a little while.</td>', 'I will not argue about whether or not this is a ''sound''. Look, I''m shutting up about it right now. It''s a very pretty photograph. I like the line of powerline poles and the dip and swap that follows the mountain for a little while.', '2003-06-04 03:37:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(314732, 23432, 8530, '<td valign="top">THANK YOU for actually having someone BLOWING the whistle.<br/> <br/>It''s another one of those shots where I wonder why black and white was chosen but it''s not as if that''s terribly distracting. It meets the challenge, it''s a good photo.</td>', 'THANK YOU for actually having someone BLOWING the whistle. It''s another one of those shots where I wonder why black and white was chosen but it''s not as if that''s terribly distracting. It meets the challenge, it''s a good photo.', '2003-06-04 03:38:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(314734, 22979, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous, well-framed, nice scarf (?) used as a background, very colourful in a way that is not too distracting. My objection is that while it is pretty art and is a reasonable concept, I really prefer that instruments in a "Sound" challenge be in use.</td>', 'This is gorgeous, well-framed, nice scarf (?) used as a background, very colourful in a way that is not too distracting. My objection is that while it is pretty art and is a reasonable concept, I really prefer that instruments in a "Sound" challenge be in use.', '2003-06-04 03:39:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(314737, 23156, 8530, '<td valign="top">At first glance I almost thought this was static but then I caught the string vibration. Because of the colour tones in the shot it doesn''t immediately draw the eye, but the more you look at it the easier it is to see it and focus on it, so overall a reasonable shot.</td>', 'At first glance I almost thought this was static but then I caught the string vibration. Because of the colour tones in the shot it doesn''t immediately draw the eye, but the more you look at it the easier it is to see it and focus on it, so overall a reasonable shot.', '2003-06-04 03:42:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(314739, 23178, 8530, '<td valign="top">Mmm... kind of conveys an idle (not idLING, but ''off'') tractor engine on first impression because of how hard it is to see the smoke against the clouds. If the smoke stood out more it would be better. Also, honestly, the horse in the background is distracting; my mind keeps saying ''Ooo, horsie!'' rather than focussing on the other things. The angle on this is probably part of the problem; the placement of the smoke is such that the bulk of the tractor (and the horsie!) keep drawing the eye away from it. (Nice horsie! Is it a working horse or one for riding or both?) (See what I mean?)<br/> <br/>That having been said, the concept is good; those things get LOUD.</td>', 'Mmm... kind of conveys an idle (not idLING, but ''off'') tractor engine on first impression because of how hard it is to see the smoke against the clouds. If the smoke stood out more it would be better. Also, honestly, the horse in the background is distracting; my mind keeps saying ''Ooo, horsie!'' rather than focussing on the other things. The angle on this is probably part of the problem; the placement of the smoke is such that the bulk of the tractor (and the horsie!) keep drawing the eye away from it. (Nice horsie! Is it a working horse or one for riding or both?) (See what I mean?) That having been said, the concept is good; those things get LOUD.', '2003-06-04 03:45:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(314740, 23386, 8530, '<td valign="top">Creepy blue lighting effect.<br/> <br/>Not sure I care for the overlapping positioning of the speakers. It does something weird to the way the curves meet up and draws the eye to this abstract little section in the center rather than the "Look, speakers!" aspect. That may just be me. I would have preferred slightly set apart, though.</td>', 'Creepy blue lighting effect. Not sure I care for the overlapping positioning of the speakers. It does something weird to the way the curves meet up and draws the eye to this abstract little section in the center rather than the "Look, speakers!" aspect. That may just be me. I would have preferred slightly set apart, though.', '2003-06-04 03:46:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(314741, 23488, 8530, '<td valign="top">Interesting candid shot. Would have preferred a focus closer on the stage, though; the picture as is tends to emphasize the audience, not the players (and therefore the ''sound'' aspect).<br/> <br/>Absolutely without any connection to anything, I''m curious if this is along the Mississippi somewhere...</td>', 'Interesting candid shot. Would have preferred a focus closer on the stage, though; the picture as is tends to emphasize the audience, not the players (and therefore the ''sound'' aspect). Absolutely without any connection to anything, I''m curious if this is along the Mississippi somewhere...', '2003-06-04 03:47:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(314743, 23407, 8530, '<td valign="top">This was another one I was expecting, though it looks on a quick glance of thumbs you''re the only one who did it, which you''re probably relieved at.<br/> <br/>Captures the topic well in part because it IS so expected. I like the pouring milk (that''s when the sound''s the loudest, after all!) and the bowl is perfectly centered left/right which is nice. It''s also a good colour combination -- blue/white cloth, blue/white bowl, blue/white cup/saucer, and the blue/yellow bo with that nice blurry neutral space between, and works well for me.<br/> <br/>Interesting to see the contents weight in grams -- must be outside the U.S. That''s totally unrelated to my impression of the picture, it was just something I noticed as I looked the photo over more closely. I guess ''snap, crackle, pop'' is more international than I thought!</td>', 'This was another one I was expecting, though it looks on a quick glance of thumbs you''re the only one who did it, which you''re probably relieved at. Captures the topic well in part because it IS so expected. I like the pouring milk (that''s when the sound''s the loudest, after all!) and the bowl is perfectly centered left/right which is nice. It''s also a good colour combination -- blue/white cloth, blue/white bowl, blue/white cup/saucer, and the blue/yellow bo with that nice blurry neutral space between, and works well for me. Interesting to see the contents weight in grams -- must be outside the U.S. That''s totally unrelated to my impression of the picture, it was just something I noticed as I looked the photo over more closely. I guess ''snap, crackle, pop'' is more international than I thought!', '2003-06-04 03:48:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(314744, 23002, 8530, '<td valign="top">Okay, that, that is cool. A very distinctive sound, yes. The motion capture is very interesting looking. Where on earth did you find a BLUE pool table? (Or is that some amount of colour adjustment? I notice the oranges and reds aren''t as sharply red as I might expect either so I''m suspecting it may be.)</td>', 'Okay, that, that is cool. A very distinctive sound, yes. The motion capture is very interesting looking. Where on earth did you find a BLUE pool table? (Or is that some amount of colour adjustment? I notice the oranges and reds aren''t as sharply red as I might expect either so I''m suspecting it may be.)', '2003-06-04 03:48:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(314745, 23306, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is a nice idea, and a very pretty photo. Cropped or framed well (whichever applies), and good choice of background.</td>', 'This is a nice idea, and a very pretty photo. Cropped or framed well (whichever applies), and good choice of background.', '2003-06-04 03:48:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(314747, 23324, 8530, '<td valign="top">While ''sound'' was not the first thing this shouted at me (no pun intended), thinking about it I realized this was a good representation of it. I like the shot, close focus on the ''talk'' button, colour/tone.</td>', 'While ''sound'' was not the first thing this shouted at me (no pun intended), thinking about it I realized this was a good representation of it. I like the shot, close focus on the ''talk'' button, colour/tone.', '2003-06-04 03:48:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(314748, 22936, 8530, '<td valign="top">Wherefore are the headphones? Is it really sound if no one can hear it? (Oh no, not that debate again.)<br/> <br/>Interesting choice, good commercial art feel.</td>', 'Wherefore are the headphones? Is it really sound if no one can hear it? (Oh no, not that debate again.) Interesting choice, good commercial art feel.', '2003-06-04 03:49:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(314749, 23378, 8530, '<td valign="top">On the one hand, I''d like to say that seeing a creative, metaphysical interpretation of ''sound'' is good. On the other hand, really, this doesn''t grab me. I''m a little weary of jingoistic photos and imagery after being bombarded with them for the last 2.5 years, so some of this is my personal thing. <br/> <br/>On the technical side, this is a good photo of Lady Liberty, framed well and taken from a good angle to hit the light. I just typoed ''angle'' twice as ''angel'', which may be a subliminal effect or may just be my entire lack of sleep.</td>', 'On the one hand, I''d like to say that seeing a creative, metaphysical interpretation of ''sound'' is good. On the other hand, really, this doesn''t grab me. I''m a little weary of jingoistic photos and imagery after being bombarded with them for the last 2.5 years, so some of this is my personal thing.  On the technical side, this is a good photo of Lady Liberty, framed well and taken from a good angle to hit the light. I just typoed ''angle'' twice as ''angel'', which may be a subliminal effect or may just be my entire lack of sleep.', '2003-06-04 03:49:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(314885, 23234, 6913, '<td valign="top">Good - would look better if we are able to see the eyes...</td>', 'Good - would look better if we are able to see the eyes...', '2003-06-04 07:56:54.000000', NULL, 1),
